# Golden fixtures are compared BYTE FOR BYTE, so git must never rewrite their line endings.
#
# Without this, a file with `text: unspecified` is auto-detected and converted on checkout wherever
# core.autocrlf is on — which is the default on GitHub's Windows runners. That is exactly how
# TestMarshalIndexMatchesTransformersGolden came to fail on windows-latest and pass everywhere
# else: the checked-in golden is LF, the checked-out copy was CRLF, and marshalIndex emits LF.
#
# The failure is invisible on Linux and macOS, so the whole class has to be prevented rather than
# fixed per test.
testdata/** -text
**/testdata/** -text

# Binary model and array formats, wherever they live.
*.safetensors -text
*.gguf -text
*.npy -text
*.npz -text
*.bin -text
*.pt -text
